    "result_text": "No documentation references. The implementation is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the derived `checkDigit` field.\n\n**What `memberId` is:** REGION (region code from postcode\u2192city) + FY (2-digit fiscal year, FY starts 1 July) + HASH8 (first 8 upper-hex of SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone + lastName` \u2014 the same HASH8 the region-and-hash identity uses) + CHK (single Luhn check digit over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`). Example produced at test time: `NSW2716E6609E1`.\n\n**Changes:**\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 replaced the `customerCode` and `checkDigit` schema properties with a single `memberId` property, and removed `membershipNumber` (the DTO regenerates from this at build time).\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 removed the `customerCode`/`membershipNumber` fields and accessors; added `memberId` (`member_id` column).\n- **`OwnerRegistrar.java`** \u2014 replaced `customerCode()`/`membershipNumber()` with a `memberId()` builder; collision handling now de-duplicates against existing `memberId`s (appending `-<n>`). Dropped the two old setters in the create pipeline.\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 removed the `checkDigit` mapping and method; `fiscalYear` now reads the FY segment out of `memberId` (falling back to `registrationDate`), and the region for `locality`/`ownerSegment` is parsed from `memberId` via a shared `memberIdCore` helper (variable-length region + fixed 11-char FY/HASH8/CHK tail).\n- **`OwnerAuditor.java`** \u2014 the human-readable audit line and the structured event now emit `memberId` as the primary identifier.\n- **Schema SQL** (h2/hsqldb/mysql/postgres) \u2014 replaced `customer_code`/`membership_number` columns with `member_id`.\n\n**Tests:** `./mvnw -o test` \u2192 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS. The acceptance test confirms `memberId` starts with `NSW`, contains the computed HASH8, and that `customerCode`/`membershipNumber` are gone.\n\nOne design note worth flagging: since REGION is variable-length (`NSW` vs `UNKNOWN`) and there are no delimiters, I parse segments by stripping the fixed 11-char `FY+HASH8+CHK` tail from the core (the core being `memberId` up to any `-<n>` disambiguation suffix). This is robust because region codes and hex contain no `-`.",
